01:47:11,182 --> 01:47:14,256
第二种是无线局域网（WLAN）。
The second type is WLAN or wireless LAN.

1092
01:47:14,638 --> 01:47:23,972
所谓无线局域网，它与普通局域网类似。它是小范围内的无线网络。它可以是购物中心、学校或机场。
So what the wireless LAN, it's similar to what a LAN is. So it's a wireless network in a small area. It could be a shopping mall, it could be school, it could be an airport.

1093
01:47:24,974 --> 01:47:27,856
我的意思是相对较小的范围，但我不是在说两米左右。
I mean relatively small, but I'm not talking about two meters.

1094
01:47:28,016 --> 01:47:35,204
它可以是多个相连的建筑，或者是一个校园内的建筑，但那就会是一个较大的无线局域网了。
I mean it can be multiple buildings even attached, or maybe a campus building, but that would be a big or a larger wireless LAN.

1095
01:47:36,014 --> 01:47:38,244
所以它就像局域网一样，只不过是无线的。
So it is like a LAN, but it is wireless.

1096
01:47:38,542 --> 01:47:42,816
也就是说，我们不需要用线把所有设备连接到网络中。
So we don't use cables to connect all the devices into the network.

1097
01:47:43,918 --> 01:47:51,696
比如当我们使用手机、笔记本电脑或平板电脑，连接到家里或办公室的 Wi-Fi 网络时。
Examples to that when we use our phone, laptops, or tablets, when we connect to the Wi-Fi network at home or in the office.

1098
01:47:51,856 --> 01:47:53,060
这就是无线局域网。
That is a wireless LAN.

1099
01:47:54,958 --> 01:47:59,216
如果按照我们讨论的内容，理论上它的结构是这样的。
And here's how it would theoretically look like if this is what we are talking about.

1100
01:47:59,376 --> 01:48:02,816
当然，我们需要一个设备，我们称之为无线路由器。
And of course, we need a device, we call it the wireless router.

1101
01:48:02,976 --> 01:48:10,496
稍后我们会讨论什么是路由器，它是为了连接互联网并为设备提供 Wi-Fi 服务。
We'll talk about what a router is later on in order to be able to connect to the internet and then provide the Wi-Fi service to the devices.

1102
01:48:10,734 --> 01:48:19,456
基本上，通过 Wi-Fi 我可以连接到路由器，而这个路由器已经连接到了互联网，因为你必须订阅网络服务
So basically, what happens is through Wi-Fi I can connect to the router, and this router is already connected to the internet because you have to subscribe to the internet

1103
01:48:19,616 --> 01:48:28,336
才能让你的家连接到互联网，对吧？你需要联系 ATT 或 Bridge Telecom，他们会为你提供 Wi-Fi 路由器和连接。
to connect your home to the internet, right? You have to call ATT or maybe Bridge Telecom, and then they will provide you with the Wi-Fi router and the connection.

1104
01:48:28,416 --> 01:48:37,936
他们可能会派技术人员过来，或者给你一套 DIY 套件，然后你安装好它，输入用户名、密码以及他们发给你的所有信息，你就连接上互联网了。
They will send in a technician maybe, or a do-it-yourself kit, and then you fix it, put the username, passwords, all the stuff that they will send you, and you are connected to the internet.

1105
01:48:38,256 --> 01:48:41,572
现在你的电脑也可以连接到互联网了。
And now your computers can connect to the internet as well.

1106
01:48:43,566 --> 01:48:50,736
接下来是广域网（WAN）。广域网络是连接远距离跨度上的计算机和网络的网络。
Then we have wide area network. So wide area network is a network that connects computers and networks over long distances.

1107
01:48:50,896 --> 01:48:59,456
比如我有一个分公司在纽约，另一个分公司在加利福尼亚，或者总部在加州，我想把它们连接起来。
So it could be that I have a branch in New York and another branch in California or the corporate in California and I would like to connect them to each other.

1108
01:48:59,630 --> 01:49:04,292
它可能跨越城市、跨越州、跨越国家，甚至跨越全球。
It could be across cities, it could be across states, across countries, or even across the globe.

1109
01:49:04,718 --> 01:49:09,924
广域网可以将许多地区连接在一起，让人们能够进行沟通、共享文件等等。
The WAN can connect many lands together so people can communicate and share files and so on.

1110
01:49:10,016 --> 01:49:11,616
这是一个例子。
And here is an example.

1111
01:49:11,886 --> 01:49:14,340
如果我们有一家公司的 LAN 分支在德国，
If we have a company LAN branch in Germany,

1112
01:49:15,086 --> 01:49:24,736
但公司的总部在美国，我们该如何连接它们？一种方法就是在它们之间建立 WAN 连接，也就是一个高速广域网连接。
but the headquarters of the company is in the US, how can we connect them? One way would be to do a WAN connection between them, a high-speed WAN connection.

1113
01:49:24,816 --> 01:49:28,068
当然，因为跨越了洲际，这肯定会很昂贵。
Of course, it's going to be costly because this is across continents.

1114
01:49:28,656 --> 01:49:36,416
然后德国的 LAN 和美国的总部 LAN 就可以通过那个 WAN 连接起来了。
And then the LAN in Germany and the headquarters LAN in the US can now be connected through that WAN.

1115
01:49:36,750 --> 01:49:44,644
我们将查看构建 LAN 的网络设备细节，以及构建 WAN 的网络设备有哪些。
We're going to look at the details of what a LAN or network devices that can build a LAN and what network devices can build a WAN.

1116
01:49:47,118 --> 01:49:53,696
既然我们在谈论 WAN，那么世界上最大的 WAN 是什么？那就是互联网。
And since we are talking about WAN, then what is the largest WAN in the world? And that is the internet.

1117
01:49:54,094 --> 01:49:57,156
所以这是世界上最大的一个。这样我就可以有
So this is our largest one in the world. So I can have

1118
01:49:58,496 --> 01:50:00,676
有人在位于日本的家庭办公室，
someone in a home office in Japan,

1119
01:50:01,902 --> 01:50:14,016
可能还有一家在德国的分支机构或公司。他们都连接到互联网上，并可以交换数据或访问托管在美国的数据。
and maybe a branch office that is in Germany, or a company that is in Germany. and they are all connected to the internet, and they can exchange data or access data that is hosted in the US.

1120
01:50:14,176 --> 01:50:16,996
例如，在公司办公室里。
for example, in the corporate office.

1121
01:50:17,326 --> 01:50:23,044
这就是我们拥有的庞大的 WAN，我们都在使用它，并且已经习惯了它。
So this is the gigantic WAN that we have, and we are all using it and we are used to it.

1122
01:50:26,894 --> 01:50:38,304
现在让我们看看流量类型的流动。当你谈论网络并有设备连接时，它们是点对点、一对多还是对所有人连接？它们是如何通信的？
Now let's look at types of traffic flow. When you are talking about a network and I have devices connected, do they connect one to one or one to many or one to everyone? How do they communicate?

1123
01:50:38,464 --> 01:50:42,980
在网络中发送流量有哪些不同的方式？
What are the different ways to send traffic in a network?

1124
01:50:43,918 --> 01:50:48,224
主要有三种类型：单播、组播和广播。
And there are three major types: unicast, multicast, and broadcast.

1125
01:50:48,304 --> 01:50:51,908
还有一种叫 AnyCast，但现在不是谈论它的时候。
There is another one called AnyCast, but it's not the time to talk about it now.

1126
01:50:52,686 --> 01:50:55,460
那么当我们谈到单播时，是什么意思？
So when we when we talk about Unicast, what do you mean?

1127
01:50:55,822 --> 01:51:07,108
如果我想连接我的银行账户或网上银行，那就是一对一，我正在与银行服务器通信，并且不与任何其他人共享这些数据。
If I want to connect to my bank account or online banking, that is one to one, I am talking to the bank server and I'm not sharing that data with anyone else.

1128
01:51:07,886 --> 01:51:16,864
所以这是点对点。就像 Sarah 和 Joan 在互相交流，她们分别在会议室里，而且没有其他人。
So this is one to one. As if Sarah and Joan are communicating with each other and they are separately in a meeting room and there is no one else.

1129
01:51:16,944 --> 01:51:28,836
这就是它们之间的点对点流量。数据从网络中的一个设备传输到特定的设备，从客户端到服务器，比如从 iPhone 到公司的 HR 服务器。
So that's one to one traffic between them. So the data goes from one device in the network to a specific device, from a client to a server, from an iPhone to the HR server, for example,

1130
01:51:29,104 --> 01:51:30,020
在公司里。
in the company.

1131
01:51:31,342 --> 01:51:32,708
然后我们有组播。
Then we have multicast.

1132
01:51:33,134 --> 01:51:35,588
组播意味着一对群组。
Multicast means one to a group.

1133
01:51:36,078 --> 01:51:39,524
例如，我可能在医院里有一个 IPTV 服务器
So it could be that I have an IPTV server

1134
01:51:40,238 --> 01:51:46,820
然后病房里的病人可以打开他们的电视。这也可以是酒店。
in a hospital, for example, and then the patients in the rooms they can turn on their TVs. It could be a hotel as well.

1135
01:51:47,182 --> 01:51:52,900
他们可以打开电视，而我可能正在看和你以及其他人都在看的同一部电影。
They can turn on in their TVs, and I could be watching the same movie that you are watching and someone else is watching.

1136
01:51:53,646 --> 01:51:55,460
所以那就是一对多。
So that would be one too many.

1137
01:51:55,824 --> 01:51:59,344
这将是组播或者流式传输给其他人。
That will be multicast or streamed to the others.

1138
01:51:59,534 --> 01:52:01,604
Netflix 也是一个这样的例子。
And Netflix is an example of that as well.

1139
01:52:02,350 --> 01:52:05,124
另一方面，广播就是一对全。
A broadcast, on the other hand, is one to all.

1140
01:52:05,344 --> 01:52:09,764
就像如果有一个公共广播系统。想象一下连接到网络上的公共广播系统
Like if there is a PA system. Think a PA system connected to the network

1141
01:52:10,702 --> 01:52:20,864
在机场。当广播或信息发出时，比如现在我们正在讨论的航线、航班号……正在登机
in an airport. So when the message is presented or the message is run, now we're talking about bridge airways, flight number such and such is boarding

1142
01:52:21,024 --> 01:52:23,204
现在，这就是某种特定的内容。
now, and that is engaged such and such.

1143
01:52:23,744 --> 01:52:31,428
任何处于该音频系统或广播系统覆盖范围内的都能听到，对吧？
Everyone who is within the reach of that audio system or a PA system will be able to hear it, right?

1144
01:52:31,694 --> 01:52:39,332
所以在网络中，如果有人发送广播，意味着该网络上的所有人都会收到这些流量。
So in networking, if one is sending a broadcast, that means everyone on that network is going to receive that traffic.

1145
01:52:45,038 --> 01:52:48,036
现在我们来谈谈有线网络设备。
Now let's talk about wired network devices.

1146
01:52:48,686 --> 01:52:57,104
如果我提到 LAN 或 WAN，在构建 LAN 时，我可能会遇到哪些常见的设备？
If I'm talking about a LAN or a WAN, what are common devices that I may come across when I am building a LAN

1147
01:52:57,264 --> 01:53:03,332
或者在构建 WAN、进行调查、故障排除、配置，甚至只是查看设计时？
or building a WAN or even investigating, troubleshooting, configuring, or even just looking at a design?

1148
01:53:03,982 --> 01:53:07,664
构建 WAN 或构建 LAN 时常用的设备有哪些？
What are the common devices that build a WAN or build a LAN?

1149
01:53:07,984 --> 01:53:09,124
这就是我们现在需要了解的。
That's what we need to know now.

1150
01:53:09,966 --> 01:53:13,732
所以，我们需要网络设备来创建 LAN 和 WAN。
So networking devices are needed to create LANs and WANs.

1151
01:53:13,838 --> 01:53:21,028
那么它们是什么？这个小气泡里有什么，而那个被称为 WAN 的小云朵里又有什么？
So what are they? What is inside this little bubble here, and what is inside that little cloud over there called a WAN?

1152
01:53:23,374 --> 01:53:29,252
第一个你可能很少遇到的设备，因为它是一种老技术，叫做集线器。
So the very first one that you may rarely encounter, because that's an old technology, is called a hub.

1153
01:53:30,702 --> 01:53:35,504
什么是集线器？它是一种在 LAN 中连接多个计算设备的网络设备。
So what's a hub? It's a network device that connects multiple computing devices in a LAN.

1154
01:53:35,744 --> 01:53:37,584
我能连接打印机吗？可以。
So can I connect a printer? Yes.

1155
01:53:37,824 --> 01:53:46,224
我能连接笔记本电脑吗？可以。能连接服务器吗？可以。能连接 CCTV 监控或监视摄像头吗？可以，这些你都能做。但它并不智能。
Can I connect a laptop? Yes. Can I connect a server? Yes. Can I connect a CCTV monitoring or surveillance camera? Yes, you can do all of that. But it is not intelligent.

1156
01:53:46,446 --> 01:53:51,492
这是一个廉价局域网（LAN）的例子。
And here's an example of how a local area network, an inexpensive one, may look like.

1157
01:53:52,814 --> 01:53:57,668
集线器的缺点是它会将数据发送到所有连接的设备上。所以它就像是一种广播。
The disadvantages of a hub, it sends data to all connected devices. So it's like a broadcast.

1158
01:53:58,064 --> 01:54:03,748
如果某个设备发出信号，比如这个笔记本电脑正尝试向打印机打印内容。
If any device sends, like let's say this laptop is trying to print something to the printer.

1159
01:54:04,910 --> 01:54:09,604
那么集线器接收到的这些流量将会被发送到集线器的所有端口上。
So that traffic that will be received by the hub is going to be sent on all ports of the hub.

1160
01:54:10,064 --> 01:54:13,184
我指的就是这些端口。
And these are ports that I'm talking about.

1161
01:54:13,264 --> 01:54:16,388
这些是我们将设备连接到上面的集线器端口。
These are the hub ports that we connect the devices to.

1162
01:54:16,878 --> 01:54:21,540
如果这是发给打印机的，它就不应该被发送到这里，也不应该被发送到这里。
If this is going to the printer, this should not have been sent here and should not have been sent here.

1163
01:54:21,998 --> 01:54:32,068
所以它浪费了带宽，浪费了媒介，或者说由于那些不需要接收这些流量的设备而导致网络媒体被无谓占用。
So it wastes the bandwidth, it wastes the media or it occupies the media of the network for unnecessary reasons for devices that don't need to receive that traffic.

1164
01:54:32,654 --> 01:54:37,092
而且它没有过滤功能，也没有智能性，它只是转发流量。仅此而已。
And there is no filtering and there is no intelligence, it's just forwards traffic. That's it.

1165
01:54:38,414 --> 01:54:40,388
所有设备都共享相同的带宽。
All devices will share the same bandwidth.

1166
01:54:40,544 --> 01:54:43,844
所以这些是集线器的主要缺点，
So these are major disadvantages of hubs,

1167
01:54:44,750 --> 01:54:47,108
而且它的性能较低，安全性也较差。
and it is lower and less secure as well.

1168
01:54:49,870 --> 01:54:55,332
我们在构建 LAN 时可能遇到的另一种网络设备类型是交换机。
Another networking device type that we may encounter when we are building LANs is a switch.

1169
01:54:56,014 --> 01:54:58,468
它是集线器的智能版本。
And that is an intelligent version of the hub.

1170
01:54:58,624 --> 01:55:02,500
它速度快得多，更智能，而且还可以进行隔离。
It is much faster and it is more intelligent and can do isolation as well.

1171
01:55:02,990 --> 01:55:08,708
这里有一个由 D-Link 公司生产的交换机示例。
And here's an example of how a switch from a company called D-Link, for example, looks like.

1172
01:55:09,104 --> 01:55:13,668
这个有 8x3，也就是 24 个端口。
So this one has 8 times 3, so that's 24 ports.

1173
01:55:14,318 --> 01:55:17,508
这里有一些 LED 指示灯。
I have here LED indicators, LED indicators.

1174
01:55:17,744 --> 01:55:23,904
当其中一个端口连接并有流量时，指示灯会闪烁，表示该端口已连接。
When one of the ports is connected and there is traffic on it will be flashing lights showing that this is connected.

1175
01:55:23,984 --> 01:55:33,264
灯的颜色可以是绿色、红色或橙色，用来指示状态：绿色代表正常运行，橙色可能意味着有一些错误，
And the light can be green, can be red, can be orange to indicate whether it green means normal operation, orange means there might be some errors,

1176
01:55:33,504 --> 01:55:39,428
红色意味着严重问题，或者可能只是关机了，没有连接。
red that means a major problem, or maybe it's just switched off, so there is no connection into it.

1177
01:55:40,078 --> 01:55:47,908
正如你看到的，每一个都是被称为端口或接口。这是我们连接电缆的交换机端口。
And as you can see, this each one of these is called a port or an interface. So this is a switch port where we have the cable connect to.

1178
01:55:49,454 --> 01:55:59,908
这些是 24 个端口，这意味着我可以物理连接 20 个设备到这个交换机上。这就是 LAN 中的交换机长什么样。
So these are 24 ports, that means I can connect physically 24 devices to this switch. So that's an example of how a switch in a LAN would look like.

1179
01:56:00,718 --> 01:56:07,424
现在，如果我开始把设备连接到它上面，每个设备都会通过物理电缆连接。
Now, if I take that and I start to connect the devices to it, so each one is going to connect through a physical cable.

1180
01:56:07,584 --> 01:56:15,012
我们稍后会讨论电缆的细节，这占用一个端口，那个占用第二个端口，第三个，第四个。
We're going to look at the details of the cables later on, and that occupies one port, that occupies a second port, third port, fourth port.

1181
01:56:15,214 --> 01:56:19,556
现在我还有 20 个端口留给额外的设备或未来的连接。
So now I have 20 ports left for extra devices or for future connectivity.

1182
01:56:20,814 --> 01:56:23,024
所以交换机可以是物理的，也可以是虚拟的。
So a switch can be physical or virtual.

1183
01:56:23,214 --> 01:56:25,264
这是一个物理交换机，我们可以看到它。
So this is a physical switch, we can see it.

1184
01:56:25,424 --> 01:56:30,692
如果它就在我面前，我还可以触摸到它。我可以给它通电，也可以往里插电缆。
And if it is in front of me, I can touch it as well. I can power it on, I can connect a cable into it.

1185
01:56:30,944 --> 01:56:33,504
但也有软件交换机。
But there are also software switches.

1186
01:56:33,664 --> 01:56:36,964
这些是虚拟交换机，我们稍后会讲到这个内容。
These are the virtual switches, and we're going to cover that as we move on.

1187
01:56:37,806 --> 01:56:42,916
与集线器相比，交换机的优势在于它只会把数据发送给目标设备。
Advantages of switches compared to hubs, it will send data only to the intended device.

1188
01:56:43,182 --> 01:56:53,344
比如在同样的场景下，如果这台笔记本想把流量发到这台打印机上，流量只会在这两个端口之间切换。
So if we have the same scenario where this laptop would like to send traffic into this printer, the traffic is going to be switched only between this port and this port.

1189
01:56:53,424 --> 01:56:55,844
所以这个不会看到它，那个也不会看到它。
So this will not see it, and this will not see it.

1190
01:56:56,224 --> 01:57:00,804
这意味着我正在对带宽进行分段。它不是共用的单一带宽。
Which means I am segmenting the bandwidth. It's not like one common bandwidth.

1191
01:57:01,294 --> 01:57:04,304
与此同时，这个正在发送到打印机。
So at the same time, this is sending to the printer.

1192
01:57:04,464 --> 01:57:13,668
比如，可能有人正坐在这个设备上，在那个显示器上播放来自摄像机的视频，它们是完全独立的，互不干扰。
It could be that someone sitting on this device is displaying the video from the camera on this monitor, for example, and they're completely separate and they don't see each other.

1193
01:57:14,670 --> 01:57:25,344
而且它更快、更安全，因为现在我们可以进行隔离，而且它也很智能。我们可以配置安全功能，每个连接都能跑满全速。
And it is faster and more secure because now we can do the isolation, it is intelligent as well. We can have security features configured, and each connection can use its full speed.

1194
01:57:25,424 --> 01:57:33,572
如果这个端口是每秒 100 兆比特或者可能是每秒 1 吉比特，那么它到交换机就是 1G 的速度，
If this port is 100 megabits per second or maybe 1 gigabits per second, so it has 1 gig speed into the switch,

1195
01:57:34,146 --> 01:57:35,684
同样地，第二个、第三个和第四个也是。
