4751
06:58:00,238 --> 06:58:05,636
一台从中国购买的带有NIC卡，即网络接口卡的笔记本电脑或服务器。
A laptop or a server that has a NIC card, a network interface card that you bought from China.

4752
06:58:05,872 --> 06:58:07,812
这台服务器是来自韩国的。
The server is from Korea.

4753
06:58:08,192 --> 06:58:17,700
然后你带入来自中国台湾的电缆，把所有这些连接起来，并连接到来自美国的交换机上，所有这些都能正常工作，没有任何问题。
And then you bring in the cable from Taiwan and you connect all of these and you connect it to the switch from the US, all of that is going to work without any problems.

4754
06:58:18,286 --> 06:58:21,392
这就是所谓的数据链路层。
This is going to be data link layer, as it is called.

4755
06:58:21,518 --> 06:58:24,644
所以它定义了交换机及相关内容的标准。
So it defines the standards for switching and related.

4756
06:58:25,518 --> 06:58:34,672
接下来是第三层。请注意，一共有七层，这就是为什么当我们说第一层、第二层、第三层、第四层、第七层时，你就会知道我们在讨论什么。
Then we have layer three. And please note that there are seven layers, and that's why when we say layer one, layer two, layer three, layer four, layer seven, you know what we are talking about.

4757
06:58:34,862 --> 06:58:43,300
所以当我们说一个设备在第七层运行时，你就应该明白它能理解所有的应用程序报头之类的东西。
So when we say that a device functions at layer seven, then you should understand that it understands all the application headers and stuff like that.

4758
06:58:44,622 --> 06:58:51,044
最重要且始终相关的层是第三层、第四层和第七层。
The most important ones that always are relevant are layer three, layer four, and layer seven.

4759
06:58:51,232 --> 06:58:54,752
你需要像背诵一样熟悉这些。它们的作用是什么？
You need to know these like the back of your hand. What do they do?

4760
06:58:54,912 --> 06:58:55,780
它们的功能是什么？
What's their function?

4761
06:58:57,710 --> 06:59:08,192
第三层是关于网络的。所以它定义了路由器、接口、路由协议、Ping命令、ICMP、IPsec的标准，
Layer three is about the network. So it defines the standards for the routers, the interfaces, the routing protocols, the ping ICMP, IPsec,

4762
06:59:08,430 --> 06:59:11,632
我们稍后会讨论如何对数据进行加密。
we'll talk about it later on for scrambling the data.

4763
06:59:11,872 --> 06:59:17,028
IP、OSPF，很多东西都会在这一层运行，
IP, OSPF, a lot of things will function at this layer

4764
06:59:17,792 --> 06:59:19,844
这些都与路由有关。
that have to do with routing.

4765
06:59:20,942 --> 06:59:24,512
然后我们进入第四层，传输层。
Then we get into the fourth one, the transport.

4766
06:59:24,752 --> 06:59:35,152
所以这是从一侧获取数据并与另一侧建立连接的通道，然后我们将数据传送到目的地。
So this is the bus that will take the data from one side and will establish a connection with the other side, and then we'll send the data down to get there.

4767
06:59:35,470 --> 06:59:40,132
这就是传输层，即两边之间需要建立的连接。
So that's the transport, the connection between the two sides that needs to be done.

4768
06:59:40,654 --> 06:59:46,948
这将定义许多我们将要讨论的内容：TCP、UDP、SSL、TLS。我们将讨论所有这些内容。
And this will define a lot of things that we are going to discuss: TCP, UDP, SSL, TLS. We are going to talk about all of these.

4769
06:59:47,726 --> 06:59:52,912
接下来是会话层，它负责控制通信。
Then we have session, which is controlling the communication.

4770
06:59:53,134 --> 06:59:57,712
你打开浏览器并与网站或
You are opening your browser and talking to the website or the

4771
06:59:58,958 --> 07:00:01,392
比如电子商务，还有 Amazon.com。
e-commerce, Amazon.com, for example.

4772
07:00:01,614 --> 07:00:05,988
那么你的应用和另一端之间的会话，是谁来管理的？
So that session between your application and the other side, who is managing that?

4773
07:00:06,192 --> 07:00:07,588
那是由会话层负责的。
That will be the session layer.

4774
07:00:08,334 --> 07:00:09,700
顺便说一下，是两边都要有的。
In the two sides, by the way.

4775
07:00:10,286 --> 07:00:11,872
接下来是表示层。
And then we have the presentation.

4776
07:00:11,952 --> 07:00:21,152
这一层定义了会话信息，以及两个端之间的会话该如何建立、如何打开和关闭，
So this one defines the session information and how the session should be between the two sides, how to open the sessions, how to close the sessions,

4777
07:00:21,312 --> 07:00:23,236
以及为此交换的消息是什么。
what are the messages exchanged for that.

4778
07:00:23,534 --> 07:00:24,964
这些都属于会话层。
This is all at the session layer.

4779
07:00:26,286 --> 07:00:36,164
然后是表示层，它决定数据应该呈现成什么样，以及为了安全是否需要进行混淆，也就是所谓的加密。我们稍后会讲到这个。
And then we have the presentation that decides how the data should look like and if there is any scrambling for security, which is called encryption. We're going to cover that later on.

4780
07:00:37,038 --> 07:00:39,952
如果需要的话，这一层就会处理这些内容。
If it is required, then this layer will take care of that.

4781
07:00:40,078 --> 07:00:48,708
接着是应用层，它定义了你是在使用 DNS、浏览器用的 HTTP，还是 HTTPS 等相关内容。
And then we have the application layer that defines if you are working with DNS, HTTP for browsers or HTTPS and all that stuff.

4782
07:00:49,538 --> 07:01:00,272
好了，每一个层级都定义了标准，以及在每一层中协议、帧或数据格式应该是怎样的。
All right, Each one of these layers define the standards and how the protocols or the frames or the format of the data should be at every single layer.

4783
07:01:00,352 --> 07:01:10,148
如何建立会话，如何建立两端之间的连接，网络应该是什么样的，以及这些报头与相关的
How to establish a session, how to establish a connection between the two sides, how the network should look like, and how every one of these headers related to these

4784
07:01:10,670 --> 07:01:17,572
服务或功能在数据包中如何标识，而且这一切都必须是统一的标准。
services or functions will be identified in the packet, and it has to be standard across everything.

4785
07:01:17,838 --> 07:01:19,072
这就是为了让
And that is how

4786
07:01:19,918 --> 07:01:23,872
端点能够毫无问题地进行通信。
the end points they will be able to communicate without any problem.

4787
07:01:24,078 --> 07:01:25,860
好的，所以这个框架
Okay, so the framework

4788
07:01:26,830 --> 07:01:35,792
包含七个易于理解的步骤，每一步都承担特定的任务，从而确保从一个端设备（比如我的笔记本电脑）
in seven understandable steps, each one doing a specific job that's for a successful communication from one end device, let's say my laptop,

4789
07:01:35,952 --> 07:01:37,412
与数据中心里的服务器进行成功的通信。
with a server in a data center.

4790
07:01:39,246 --> 07:01:42,832
当数据包开始传输时，它会从用户端开始。
The packet as it starts, it will start at the user.

4791
07:01:43,150 --> 07:01:52,432
所以用户会打开浏览器，比如，不一定是浏览器，也可以是客户端，比如 Uber 应用或者 Google Maps，
So the user will open the browser, let's say, for example, it doesn't have to be a browser, it could be a client, Uber, for example, Uber application or Google Maps,

4792
07:01:52,592 --> 07:01:54,372
然后去连接 Google 服务器。
and going to the Google server.

4793
07:01:56,142 --> 07:02:03,076
所以用户在这里开始操作，这就是有效载荷，也就是数据本身。
So the user will start whatever he is doing here or she's doing here, and that will be the payload, the data itself.

4794
07:02:04,110 --> 07:02:06,916
那么在 TCP 协议栈中，
So the stack of TCP,

4795
07:02:07,888 --> 07:02:14,724
或者说在你或他电脑里的、与网络相关的服务堆栈中，
or the stack of services that have to do with networks inside your laptop, or her laptop, or his laptop,

4796
07:02:15,568 --> 07:02:24,368
应用层会开始接收这些数据，然后决定要添加哪些报头以及如何促进
the application layer is going to start getting that data and then deciding on what headers are going to be added and how to facilitate

4797
07:02:24,528 --> 07:02:25,956
它在网络中的访问。
its access to the network.

4798
07:02:27,086 --> 07:02:32,768
表示层会检查：是否需要混淆？是否需要添加相关的报头？
The presentation layer will look. Do we need any scrambling? Do we need to add any headers that relates to that?

4799
07:02:32,848 --> 07:02:36,964
然后会话层将决定会话的形式并管理这个会话。
And then the session layer will decide how the session would be and will manage the session.

4800
07:02:37,646 --> 07:02:43,968
所以这三个层级会以正确的方式准备数据，以便发送到另一端。
So these three are going to prepare the data the right way so it will be sent to the other side.

4801
07:02:44,128 --> 07:02:49,188
是否需要加密，是否不需要加密，该如何呈现，是否需要添加任何报头等等。
If it needs scrambling, if it doesn't need scrambling, how it should look like, if there are any headers to be added, and so on.

4802
07:02:50,862 --> 07:02:55,844
然后就进入到执行传输层功能的环节了。
Then it gets down to the function that does the transport layer.

4803
07:02:56,128 --> 07:02:59,396
我们现在讨论的所有内容都在笔记本电脑里。
Everything we are talking about right now is inside the laptop.

4804
07:03:00,398 --> 07:03:04,848
所以我们不是在研究架子上的各种层级，这些全都在笔记本电脑里。
So we're not going to go through layers in shelves and all that. It's all inside the laptop.

4805
07:03:04,928 --> 07:03:14,528
请想象一下，在笔记本电脑的软件和硬件中，有相应的组件来执行这些功能。是哪个组件呢？
So please use your imagination that there are components in the software and hardware in the laptop that are going to do these functions. Which component?

4806
07:03:14,688 --> 07:03:15,172
谁在乎呢？
Who cares?

4807
07:03:16,206 --> 07:03:27,364
你现在不是软件开发人员，你才刚起步。也许在未来的某个时候，你会深入了解这些，并开始针对这些不同的功能进行开发。
You are not the software developer right now, you are just starting. Maybe later on in the future, you will understand this very well and you will start developing to these different functions.

4808
07:03:28,270 --> 07:03:37,220
但目前，我们的每一个设备中都有这些功能，甚至你的手机，无论是 iPhone 还是 Android，都具备这些功能。
But for now, these functions exist in every one of our devices, even your your phone, iPhone or Android, it does have all of that.

4809
07:03:39,342 --> 07:03:46,756
这就是你笔记本电脑、手机或 iPad 里的 IP 协议栈或 TCP/IP 协议栈，它会来处理这些。好的。
This is the IP stack or the TCP IP stack inside your laptop or phone or iPad that will be doing this. Okay.

4810
07:03:47,246 --> 07:03:50,628
现在传输层需要添加报头。
Now the transport layer needs to add headers.

4811
07:03:50,768 --> 07:03:56,068
为什么？因为它是从这里到那里的传输，也就是传到另一端。
Why? Because it is the transport from here to there to the other side.

4812
07:03:56,526 --> 07:03:57,796
是直接发送吗？不是的。
Is it directly? No.

4813
07:03:58,128 --> 07:04:01,860
但它必须添加报头，这样另一端才能理解。
But it has to add headers so the other side will understand.

4814
07:04:02,190 --> 07:04:04,100
我们是否需要建立连接？
Do we need to open a connection or not?

4815
07:04:04,750 --> 07:04:09,328
我们需要遵循每个数据包的顺序吗？如果漏掉了一个，我需要通知你。
Do we need to follow the sequence of each packet? So if one is missed, then I need to tell you.

4816
07:04:09,488 --> 07:04:13,988
我们需要流量控制吗？如果你发送的内容太多，我需要让你慢一点。
Do we need to have flow control? So if you are sending too much, I need to slow you down.

4817
07:04:14,478 --> 07:04:21,636
我们是否需要额外的通信，基本上是为了确保没有任何内容丢失、没有错误接收或顺序错乱？
Do we need to have extra communication basically to ensure that there is nothing missed, nothing is received in error or out of sequence?

4818
07:04:21,888 --> 07:04:25,348
如果任何内容丢失了，我们可以沟通，你可以重新发送。
And if anything is missed, then we can talk and you can resend it again.

4819
07:04:25,966 --> 07:04:29,808
如果我们需要这样做，或者我直接把我要发的东西发给你，你收就行。
If we need to do that, or just I will send you whatever I will send, receive it.

4820
07:04:29,998 --> 07:04:31,556
如果漏掉了点什么，谁在乎呢？
And if we miss anything, who cares?

4821
07:04:32,398 --> 07:04:36,356
当涉及到传输层时，这两种都是有效的选项。
And both of these are valid options when it gets to a transport layer.

4822
07:04:36,910 --> 07:04:46,048
所以那个传输层会添加它自己的报头、各种片段，然后我们把它传过去。好，现在是时候通过网络发送了。
So that transport is going to add its own headers, the bits and pieces, and we'll deliver it. Okay, now it's time to ship it through the network.

4823
07:04:46,128 --> 07:04:47,088
那我们需要做什么？
So what do we need to do?

4824
07:04:47,342 --> 07:04:55,556
我们需要把它交给那个理解路由、了解 IP 地址以及了解 BGP（如果需要的话）和其他相关内容的层。
We need to give it to the layer that understands routing and understands IP addresses and understands BGP, for example, if that's required, and other stuff.

4825
07:04:56,608 --> 07:04:59,268
网络地址转换也发生在这一层。
network address translation also happens at this layer.

4826
07:04:59,822 --> 07:05:01,008
我们需要添加报头吗？
Do we need to add headers?

4827
07:05:01,168 --> 07:05:01,700
当然需要。
Of course.

4828
07:05:02,190 --> 07:05:05,380
那个报头存在，而这是我们原始的数据。
That header exists, and here's our original data.

4829
07:05:05,902 --> 07:05:07,488
现在增加了一个 IP 报头。
And now an IP header is added.

4830
07:05:07,648 --> 07:05:11,844
添加了源、目的 IP 地址，以及如果还需要其他内容的话。
Source, destination, IP addresses are added, and if anything else is needed.

4831
07:05:12,238 --> 07:05:17,508
在传输层，这里也会包含源端口和目的端口。
At the transport, this is the source port and destination port will be there as well.

4832
07:05:19,088 --> 07:05:20,516
通过交换机。
Goes through the switch.

4833
07:05:20,846 --> 07:05:31,140
为了让交换机能分发到同一个局域网中的不同设备，可能还会添加一些报头。这些被称为数据链路层、链路层或链路层报头。
For the switch to deliver to the different ones in the same local area network, then probably headers are going to be added also. These are called data link or link layer or link to headers.

4834
07:05:32,750 --> 07:05:40,688
完成后，它就准备好通过下一张网卡进入网络，进入局域网，然后可能到达另一个
Once this is done, it is ready now to go out on the next card to the network, to the local area network, and then possibly to the another

4835
07:05:40,928 --> 07:05:42,052
路由器之类的设备。
router or something.

4836
07:05:43,758 --> 07:05:53,348
所以，如果你是用 iPhone 通过 Wi-Fi 连接，它必须转换为无线局域网中的频率信号。
So it will filter down to now if you are holding your iPhone connected through Wi-Fi, then this has to be converted into frequencies in the wireless LAN.

4837
07:05:54,734 --> 07:06:03,568
如果它是连接到交换机的有线铜缆端口，它就会被转换为电信号，通过铜线发送。
If this was a wired copper port into a switch, then it will be converted into electrical signals to be sent through the copper wire.

4838
07:06:03,648 --> 07:06:09,636
如果是光纤或光缆，它就会被转换为光信号进行传输。
If it was optical cable, fiber optic cable, then it will be converted into light signals to be sent.

4839
07:06:09,902 --> 07:06:12,036
谁来负责这些？这就是物理层。
Who is going to do that? That is the physical layer.

4840
07:06:13,742 --> 07:06:20,836
所以从源端的应用层到到达物理层的这一路径被称为封装。
So this path from the source from the application until it gets to the physical layer is called encapsulation.

4841
07:06:21,134 --> 07:06:30,368
为什么这么叫？因为我们有数据，想象一下我们在它外面包裹了多少层东西，就像最后套上了一个胶囊一样。我们正在对数据进行封装。
Why is that? Because we have the data and imagine how many times we have added things around it as if it is a capsule at the end. We are encapsulating the data.

4842
07:06:30,448 --> 07:06:34,596
我们包含了数据，但在其周围添加了大量的报头。
We are including the data but adding a lot of headers around it.

4843
07:06:35,694 --> 07:06:43,972
现在它变成了一系列二进制的 0 和 1，无论是以电信号、光信号还是其他方式呈现。
Now it gets as a series of binary zeros and ones, either presented as electrical signals or light signals or however.

4844
07:06:44,590 --> 07:06:51,172
它到达了另一端。这里的物理层需要执行相反的过程：解封装。
It gets to the other side. The physical layer here, it needs to do the reverse process de-encapsulation.

4845
07:06:52,302 --> 07:06:59,808
所以这里的物理层会将这些转换成数据链路层可以接受的格式。
So the physical layer here is going to translate that into what is acceptable for the data link layer.

4846
07:06:59,888 --> 07:07:08,772
这样，数据链路层就能读取到数据链路所需的所有信息并进行理解，从而判断这是发给我的还是给别人的。
So the data link layer will be able to read any information required for the data link and comprehend it and find out if it is for me or for someone else,

4847
07:07:09,168 --> 07:07:16,288
然后它会移除第二层的报头，并将其传递给网络层。
then it's going to remove layer two headers and it's going to pass it on to the network layer.

4848
07:07:16,448 --> 07:07:21,088
网络层将查看源 IP 和目的 IP，确定这是发往何处的。
The network layer will look at the source and destination IP where this is going.

4849
07:07:21,326 --> 07:07:23,328
如果是发给我的，我就会处理它，否则……
If it is to me, I will process it else.

4850
07:07:23,408 --> 07:07:25,604
如果我是一个路由器，那么我就把它转发出去。
If I'm a router, then I'm going to send it.

4851
07:07:26,158 --> 07:07:31,620
如果它是路由器，它会在这一层结束，且上方不会有太多信息。
If it is a router, it will end at this layer and it will not have a lot of information above.

4852
07:07:33,774 --> 07:07:46,052
现在，如果这是我们展示的服务器，它会将其传递给传输层进行解析。好的，这原本是打算作为面向连接的通信还是无连接的？
Now, if this was the server as we are showing here, then it will pass it on to the transport layer to understand. Okay, was that supposed to be a connection-oriented communication or connectionless?

4853
07:07:46,926 --> 07:07:51,248
我们是否需要查看排序等相关信息？
Do we need to look at the sequencing and all that or not?

4854
07:07:51,438 --> 07:07:54,468
如果某些内容缺失了，我们是否需要进行重传？
Do we need to do retransmission or not if something is missing?

4855
07:07:54,894 --> 07:08:02,180
并且它会识别目标协议或端口。例如，它是去往 HTTP 80 还是端口 80？
And it understands the protocol or the port it's going to. Is it going to HTTP 80, for example, or port 80?

4856
07:08:02,382 --> 07:08:10,848
如果它前往端口 80，那么在处理完成后，它会移除每一层报头，只保留上层的
If it is going to port 80, then it will remove each one after it does the processing, it will remove the header and will leave the up

4857
07:08:11,022 --> 07:08:12,740
上层报头。
the headers for the layers above.

4858
07:08:13,518 --> 07:08:16,448
如果这是一个路由器，那么路由器就会将其转发。
If this was a router, then the router will pass it on.

4859
07:08:16,782 --> 07:08:25,168
所以我们会处理网络层，查看所需的过滤条件，然后将其传递给下一个路由器、其他设备或最终的服务器。但这不是我们目前的情况。
So we'll process the network layer, we'll look at any filtering required, and then it will pass it on to the next router or the other or to the server at the end. But this is not our case.

4860
07:08:25,328 --> 07:08:32,516
我们使用的是一个简单的案例，即两者距离很近。中间没有集线器或其他设备。
We're using a simple case that they are both close to each other. There are no hubs or no devices in between.

4861
07:08:33,326 --> 07:08:40,996
现在它向上传输，会话层读取信息，然后到表示层，接着进入应用层。
So now it goes up, session layer reads the information, presentation layer, and then it goes to the application layer.

4862
07:08:41,328 --> 07:08:49,764
这里的应用程序将理解这些内容，当它发出响应时，该应用程序就变成了发送方，
Now the application here will understand it, and then the application will become when it for the response, it will become the sender,

4863
07:08:50,062 --> 07:08:51,408
而这里就是接收方。
and here will be the receiver.

4864
07:08:51,502 --> 07:09:01,648
所以就像是我们要反转功能：对于响应来说是封装，而在笔记本电脑端对响应进行解封装。
So as if we are going to reverse the functions, encapsulation for the response, and then de-encapsulation at the laptop level for the response.

4865
07:09:01,838 --> 07:09:03,236
这就是它发生的具体过程。
So that's exactly how it happens.

4866
07:09:03,598 --> 07:09:12,740
如果我们没有这些标准，也没有把不同的功能模块化，那么任何设备内部的 TCP/IP协议栈都会变成一场噩梦。
If we didn't have all the standards and we did modularize the different functionalities, the TCP IP stack inside any device would have been a nightmare.

4867
07:09:13,166 --> 07:09:23,588
但现在，既然我们将这些拆分为功能和标准等内容，公司就可以专注于只做数据的加密功能了，
But now, since we have broken these into functions and standards and all that, it's easy for a company, for example, to specialize in only doing the scrambling function of data

4868
07:09:24,750 --> 07:09:32,288
或者比如在传输层部署一种新协议，或者在传输层实现一个新功能。
or only a deployment of a new protocol at the transport layer, for example, or a new function at the transport layer.

4869
07:09:32,526 --> 07:09:39,204
这样他们就能聚焦或深入到特定的功能上，只为那个功能进行开发。
So they can focus or zoom into a specific functionality and develop for that functionality only.

4870
07:09:41,134 --> 07:09:49,060
源软件会从应用中获取数据，向下流经不同的层直到物理层。这被称为封装。
So the source software will take the data from the application, flows down through the different layers to the physical layer. This is called encapsulation.

4871
07:09:49,488 --> 07:09:54,528
而在接收端，我们做相反的操作，这被称为解封装。
And then at the receiving end, we do the opposite, which is called de encapsulation.

4872
07:09:54,608 --> 07:09:59,940
从物理层向上是解封装，从应用层向下是封装。
From the physical up is de encapsulation, from the application down is encapsulation.

4873
07:10:02,990 --> 07:10:09,120
举个例子。假设一个用户要打开浏览器，并需要访问服务器上的一个网页。
Here's an example. Let's say a user is going to open a browser and needs to get to a web page on the server.

4874
07:10:09,422 --> 07:10:10,148
那会发生什么？
So what happens?

4875
07:10:11,534 --> 07:10:18,500
浏览器会发送 HTTP 请求，这是应用层执行的层 7 活动。
So the browser will send the HTTP request that is a layer 7 activity which is done by the application layer.

4876
07:10:20,142 --> 07:10:27,236
还有 HTTP，我们稍后会讨论这个。这是一个在层 7定义的标准协议。
and HTTP, and we are going to talk about this. This is a standard protocol that is defined at layer 7.

4877
07:10:27,598 --> 07:10:28,720
它会创建请求。
Will create the request.

4878
07:10:28,800 --> 07:10:35,780
比如，为了读取网站的 HTML 文件而发送一个 GET 请求。
Like for example, get for me a GET request to read the HTML file of the website.

4879
07:10:36,782 --> 07:10:38,820
简单来说，就是获取该网站的网页。
So the web page of the website, simply.

4880
07:10:39,534 --> 07:10:44,164
但这仍然是层 7，而且这一切现在都在……
But this is still layer 7, and this is all happening now at whatever

4881
07:10:44,814 --> 07:10:50,724
在发送方或客户端内部由浏览器功能来处理。
the browser functionality that will take care of that inside the sender or the client.

4882
07:10:52,622 --> 07:10:54,084
现在 HTTP 数据
Now the HTTP data

4883
07:10:54,958 --> 07:11:00,164
被交给层 4 的 TCP，也就是传输层。
is handed to the to TCP at layer 4, which is the transport layer.

4884
07:11:01,422 --> 07:11:10,080
它会添加一个 TCP 报头，这包含了浏览器在经过会话和表示层处理后准备好的数据。
Which adds a TCP header that includes so this is the data after the browser has prepared it with session and presentation.

4885
07:11:10,446 --> 07:11:13,444
现在到了传输层。传输层将添加 TCP 报头。
Now it gets to transport. Transport will add the TCP header.

4886
07:11:14,318 --> 07:11:15,876
什么是 TCP？我们稍后会讨论。
What is TCP? We'll talk about that.

4887
07:11:16,686 --> 07:11:18,820
它会讨论什么是源端口。
It will talk about what is the source port.

4888
07:11:19,918 --> 07:11:21,120
一个随机端口。
A random port.

4889
07:11:22,126 --> 07:11:23,876
我们稍后会讨论这些端口。
We'll talk about these ports later on.

4890
07:11:24,240 --> 07:11:28,004
目的端口对于 HTTP 将是 80 端口。
Destination port is going to be to be port 80 for HTTP.

4891
07:11:28,494 --> 07:11:37,440
所以传输层会确定谁是源端口、源应用程序、客户端应用程序，以及另一侧服务器上的目的端口。
So now the transport is saying who is the source port, source application, client application, and what is the destination port on the server on the other side.

4892
07:11:38,080 --> 07:11:39,940
这就是端口号出现的地方。
This is where the port number appears.

4893
07:11:40,080 --> 07:11:47,332
然后它向下到网络层（网络层）的 IP 来添加源 IP 和目的 IP，再到数据链路层（数据链路层），然后进入网络。
And then it goes down to layer 3 IP to add the source IP and destination IP, layer 2, and then out to the network.

4894
07:11:47,726 --> 07:11:51,396
所以希望这能结合之前的幻灯片让内容更清晰。
So hopefully this makes it clear in addition to the previous slide.

4895
07:11:53,200 --> 07:11:55,140
这样做有什么好处？
What are the benefits of doing that?

4896
07:11:55,662 --> 07:11:58,212
标准化和互操作性。
Standardization and interoperability.

4897
07:11:58,830 --> 07:12:01,764
这允许所有的软件和硬件厂商
And that allows all software and hardware vendors

4898
07:12:02,478 --> 07:12:05,252
生产出具有互操作性的产品。
to make products that are interoperable.

4899
07:12:05,934 --> 07:12:11,108
这是分层故障排除。当你有关于网络的问题时，就去查网络。
It's a layered troubleshooting. When you have a problem that has to do with a network, go and look at the network.

4900
07:12:11,662 --> 07:12:20,708
当你遇到与端口相关的问题，比如允许的流量被拦截时，我们就去查看传输层或相关的配置。
When you have a problem that has to do with ports, not allowed allowed traffic is blocked, then we go and look at the transport or configurations that have to do with the transport.

4901
07:12:21,006 --> 07:12:30,564
这样我们在修复问题时可以专注于特定的层，而不是如果所有功能都混在一起，我们该查哪一部分？
So we can focus on specific layers while fixing problems, as opposed to if it was all one big function, then which part should we look into?

4902
07:12:31,342 --> 07:12:33,764
这是更简单的网络实现方式
It's an easier implementation of networking

4903
07:12:34,798 --> 07:12:42,436
因为它更容易拆解、理解并处理不同的网络组件。模块化也非常重要。
because it's easier to break down, understand, and work with networking components, different components. Modularity is very important as well.

4904
07:12:42,766 --> 07:12:52,000
它允许较小的公司或某些公司专注于优化这七层中的某些功能或模块。
So it allows smaller companies or some companies to specialize in optimizing some of the functionalities or modules within the seven layers.

4905
07:12:53,774 --> 07:13:03,920
现在让我们深入研究一些重要的层，我们将重点关注应用层、传输层和网络层，因为这些在你的职业生涯中非常关键，你会经常接触到它们，
Let's now zoom into some of the important layers and we'll focus on layer seven, four, and three, because these ones are very critical and you will deal with them a lot in your career,

4906
07:13:04,080 --> 07:13:11,652
无论你从事什么岗位，尤其是如果你从事云工程、网络安全或网络工程。
regardless what that is, and especially if you are into cloud engineering, network security, or network engineering.

4907
07:13:12,846 --> 07:13:22,800
在 OSI 模型层中，我们有应用层，它会按我们提到的方式准备数据。我们有表示层，它负责对数据进行格式化，并在需要时进行混淆或加密。
The OSI model layers, we have the application which will prepare the data as we mentioned. We have the presentation that will format and scramble or encrypt the data if required.

4908
07:13:23,054 --> 07:13:33,520
我们有传输层，它确保消息完整且按顺序到达接收者。
We have the session that will start and stop the sessions to the receivers. We have the transport that will ensure the message will get to the receiver fully and in sequence if required.

4909
07:13:33,760 --> 07:13:44,612
我们有网络层，它负责在网络中寻找最佳路径，即 IP 路由。我们还有数据链路层，它会在交换机级别或 LAN 级别添加传输详情。
We have the network that will find the best path, the IP routing, through the network. We have the data link layer that will add the delivery details at the switch level or the LAN level, if you will.

4910
07:13:44,910 --> 07:13:51,600
物理层则为电缆、Wi-Fi 或承载数据的信号确定标准。
Physical layer that will identify standards for the cables and if it is Wi-Fi or signals that will carry the data.

4911
07:13:51,694 --> 07:13:56,420
所以这是对每一层功能的简要定义。
So this is an abbreviated definition of the function of each one of the layers.

4912
07:13:58,958 --> 07:14:02,276
让我们深入研究应用层（应用层）。
Let's zoom into layer 7, the application layer.

4913
07:14:02,720 --> 07:14:09,840
当然，应用层离最终用户最近，因为它会被构建到浏览器中，例如。
So the application layer is the closest to the end user, of course, because we said it will be built into the browser, for example.

4914
07:14:09,920 --> 07:14:16,228
这就是客户端所在的位置，也就是他们面前的浏览器，他们从这里开始操作。
So this is where the client sits, and that's the browser in front of him or her, and they start working on it.

4915
07:14:16,480 --> 07:14:26,800
这是用户与应用程序交互的地方，而应用层并不是指应用程序本身，而是其中的一项功能，
So this is where the users will interact with the applications, and this will provide the application layer, is not the application itself, it's a functionality within

4916
07:14:27,040 --> 07:14:31,200
它存在于浏览器中，处理你想要的数据。比如你想去 CNN.com。
the browser that will take the data that you want. You want to go to CNN.com.

4917
07:14:31,374 --> 07:14:38,820
它会接收这个请求，并将其转换为：当我想要访问 CNN.com 时，数据应该是什么样子的。
So it will take that and it will translate it into how should the data look like when I want to go to CNN.com.

4918
07:14:39,280 --> 07:14:45,412
它为浏览器、邮件客户端和文件传输等应用程序提供网络服务。
So it will provide network services to the applications like browsers or email clients and file transfer.

4919
07:14:47,264 --> 07:14:55,876
它不是应用本身，而是提供服务让应用能够使用网络或在网络上运行。
And it's not the application itself, but provides the services to allow the application to use the network or to work over the network.

4920
07:14:56,144 --> 07:15:04,624
它将处理发送者和接收者之间，或者用户与其他用户之间的请求和响应操作。
And it will handle the requests and the response operations between the sender and receiver or the user and the other

4921
07:15:04,864 --> 07:15:07,424
通过处理底层网络来处理。
side by handling the lower layers.

4922
07:15:07,566 --> 07:15:16,064
所以，在用户端应用和用户侧可用的底层之间，它能正确地到达另一端。
So between the user applications and the lower layers that are available at the user side so it can get to the other side correctly.

4923
07:15:16,334 --> 07:15:23,908
所以把第7层看作是让像 Chrome 或 Outlook 这样的应用能够使用网络的层
So think of the layer 7 as the layer that will let the applications like Chrome or Outlook use the network

4924
07:15:24,944 --> 07:15:32,036
通过笔记本电脑、iPhone 或安卓手机，通过网络直到到达正确的位置。
through the laptop or the iPhone or the Android phone through the network until it gets to the right place.

4925
07:15:32,224 --> 07:15:33,504
这就是第7层。
That's layer 7.

4926
07:15:33,824 --> 07:15:44,420
任何具备理解第7层发生了什么的智能的设备，通常都是昂贵且高级的设备。
Any device that has the intelligence of understanding what's happening in layer 7 is usually an expensive device and it's an advanced device.

4927
07:15:46,464 --> 07:15:50,436
接下来我们要讨论传输层，也就是第4层。
Next one we're going to discuss transport layer, layer number 4.

4928
07:15:51,024 --> 07:15:57,572
这一层在两个通信主机之间、在发送者和接收者之间建立端到端的传输。
This layer creates the end-to-end transport between the two communicating hosts, between the sender and receiver.

4929
07:15:58,126 --> 07:16:01,824
端口就在这里被添加并解析或读取。
The ports are added and interpreted or read here.

4930
07:16:02,126 --> 07:16:08,004
所以当一方说我是来自端口 55000 的源时，该端口将在传输层被添加。
So when one says I'm from port 55,000 as a source, the port will be added at the transport layer.

4931
07:16:08,464 --> 07:16:12,356
还有它要去哪里，它要前往 CNN.com 的 80 端口。
And also where it is going, it's going to CNN.com on port 80.

4932
07:16:12,944 --> 07:16:18,852
然后目的端口也会在这里被识别，并添加到 TCP 报头中。
Then the destination port is going to be also identified here and then added in the TCP header.

4933
07:16:20,174 --> 07:16:24,544
接下来我们有第三个需要深入了解的层，即网络层。
Then we have the third layer that we need to zoom into, which is the network layer.

4934
07:16:24,784 --> 07:16:30,468
正如我们所理解的，它基本上就是 IP 层。这是这里运行的主要协议。
And as we understand, it's the IP layer basically. This is the main protocol that operates here.

4935
07:16:30,926 --> 07:16:36,704
它将数据在两个没有物理连接的主机之间传输。
And it will move the data between the two hosts that are not physically connected.

4936
07:16:37,024 --> 07:16:40,784
所以它会做出路由决策，决定该怎么做。
So it will do the routing decisions, what to do.

4937
07:16:41,024 --> 07:16:49,252
是在同一个网络还是不同的网络？我需要把它发给路由器还是可以通过交换机到达？所有这些智能处理都在这一层发生。
Is it in the same network on a different network? Do I need to send it to the router or it will be reachable through the switch? All of that intelligence happens at this layer.

4938
07:16:50,030 --> 07:17:00,356
它使用逻辑 IP 地址。因此源和目的 IP 地址将在这里添加。我们还有来自传输层的源端口和目的端口。
And it uses the logical IP addressing. So the source and destination IP addresses are going to be added here. And we have the source port and destination port from the transport layer.

4939
07:17:01,024 --> 07:17:07,588
这里功能的例子还包括 IPsec、网络地址转换以及动态路由协议。
Examples of what functions here also is IPsec, network address translation, and dynamic routing protocols.

4940
07:17:08,302 --> 07:17:10,384
希望这些内容容易理解。
Hopefully that was easy to understand.

4941
07:17:10,638 --> 07:17:20,864
OSI 模型非常重要。如果你因为任何原因没搞清楚它，至少要知道第3层、第4层和第7层是干什么的。
The OSI layer is very, very important. And if you don't get your head around it for whatever reason, know what layer 3, layer 4, and layer 7 are for.

4942
07:17:21,104 --> 07:17:27,492
因为如果你不理解它们，这些内容在以后会经常成为你前进道路上的障碍。
Because these ones are going to come and as bumps in your way if you don't understand them very frequently.

4943
07:17:30,446 --> 07:17:38,564
那么我们讨论过的 OSI 模型与 TCP/IP 模型有什么关系？有一种模型叫 TCP/IP。
So the OSI model that we have discussed how is that related to the TCP IP model? There is a model called TCP IP.

4944
07:17:39,246 --> 07:17:42,404
OSI 模型与网络设备之间有什么关系？
What is the relation of the OSI model also to the network devices?

4945
07:17:44,814 --> 07:17:48,388
对于网络设备，它们在 OSI 层中处于什么位置？
So for networking devices, where do they function at the OSI layer?

4946
07:17:50,094 --> 07:17:53,156
路由器将在网络层运行。
So routers will operate at the network layer.

4947
07:17:54,030 --> 07:17:57,412
交换机将在数据链路层运行，即第2层。
And switches will operate at the data link layer, which is layer two.

4948
07:17:57,984 --> 07:18:04,292
稍后当我们讨论防火墙时，你会看到它们可能在这里工作，也可能在这一层工作。我们稍后会讨论那个。
And we'll see later on when we talk about firewalls, they could be functioning here or they could be functioning here as well. We'll talk about that later on.

4949
07:18:06,190 --> 07:18:07,876
TCP/IP 模型
The TCP IP model

4950
07:18:09,006 --> 07:18:11,236
也是为了相同的目的而构建的。
is also built for the same purpose.

4951
07:18:12,142 --> 07:18:18,660
但 TCP/IP 模型将这三层合并为一层，称为应用层。
But the TCP IP model combines these three layers into one layer called the application layer.

4952
07:18:19,822 --> 07:18:26,148
然后我们有传输层、网络层，而物理层和数据链路层被称为网络接入层。
And then we have the transport, we have the network, and the physical and data link layer are called the network access layer.

4953
07:18:27,118 --> 07:18:30,084
所以这里有四层，而这里有七层。
So here we have four layers, here we have seven layers.

4954
07:18:33,358 --> 07:18:46,112
现在让我们从 TCP/IP 协议开始。让我们了解什么是协议，为什么它很重要，以及在你的职业生涯中经常会遇到的一些常用协议，
Now let's start with TCPIP protocols. Let's understand what is a protocol and why is that important and some common protocols that we are going to come across frequently in your career,

4955
07:18:46,702 --> 07:18:49,284
无论是网络还是其他任何东西。
whether it is network or anything else.

4956
07:18:52,078 --> 07:18:54,244
首先，什么是协议？
So, first of all, what is a protocol?

4957
07:18:54,830 --> 07:18:57,348
协议是一套标准的规则。
A protocol is a standard set of rules.

4958
07:18:58,670 --> 07:19:02,852
也就是说，为了什么目的而达成了一系列记录在案的规则？
So there are a number of documented rules agreed upon for what?

4959
07:19:03,598 --> 07:19:10,832
在网络中，是为了格式化和处理数据，让计算设备知道如何发送消息。
In networking, for formatting and processing data that computing devices need to know how to send messages.

4960
07:19:10,992 --> 07:19:18,788
所以这些被公认并在全球范围内标准化的一套规则或协议，
So this set of rules or protocols agreed upon in a protocol that is known and standardized across the globe

4961
07:19:19,472 --> 07:19:24,676
将允许计算设备理解它们应该如何发送消息。
will allow the computing devices understand how they should send messages.

4962
07:19:26,158 --> 07:19:36,580
比如如何创建它们，使用哪些报头，每个报头的长度是多少，哪个放在前面，哪个放在后面，有效载荷前要放什么，有效载荷后要放什么。
So how to create them, which headers, what is the length of each header, which one to put before the others, which one to put after the payload, which one to use before the payload.

4963
07:19:37,072 --> 07:19:47,312
